	"note": "Heads taken: twenty thousand in the Zizhi Tongjian and the New Book of Tang, ten thousand in the Old Book of Tang (the Samguk Sagi's figure is garbled). The split between Go Yeonsu and Go Hyejin is not recorded and is drawn nearly even; of the Mohe, only the 3,300 buried afterwards are counted. What became of the ninety-odd thousand who neither died nor surrendered is not said; they simply leave the map. The records say the bridges were pulled down; the story burns them. The battlefield is unidentified; the ground follows the order of battle, and the forty-li line is drawn shorter.",
